From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:44:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 037/342] Debugger: arm64 support

ArchitectureARM64 and CpuStateARM64 for the arm64 debug CPU state (x0-x30,
sp, pc, cpsr), with DWARF register numbers as register indices:
- the call frame information's return address column is the link
  register, so an unwound CPU state has no pc and the caller continues
  at its lr;
- frames without call frame information come from the frame records;
- PLT entries (adrp/ldr x17/br) are followed for stepping into calls;
- four watchpoints of up to eight bytes, reads and/or writes.

DisassemblerARM64 decodes branches itself and gets the text from
Capstone, which the capstone build feature provides (only arm64 builds
include the architecture). Core files of arm64 teams can be loaded.

Architecture::CreateStackTrace() now stops when unwinding returns the
same CPU state: a loop there (as with a register order bug while porting)
grew the Debugger until the system ran out of memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
